1
00:00:02,065 --> 00:00:05,027
[♪ theme music playing]

2
00:00:27,632 --> 00:00:31,053
THE HUSBAND

3
00:00:35,307 --> 00:00:36,433
THIS SERIES IS FICTITIOUS

4
00:00:36,516 --> 00:00:39,144
CHILDREN WERE FILMED SAFELY
GEN AI WAS USED IN SELECT SCENES

5
00:00:42,481 --> 00:00:44,316
EPISODE 10

6
00:01:16,264 --> 00:01:17,849
[keypad beeping]

7
00:01:20,018 --> 00:01:21,561
[chimes]

8
00:01:26,983 --> 00:01:29,152
[door chimes]

9
00:01:38,912 --> 00:01:40,163
[sighs]

10
00:01:43,250 --> 00:01:44,251
[worker 1] Let's go.

11
00:01:44,334 --> 00:01:45,585
Yeah, I'm coming.

12
00:01:45,669 --> 00:01:46,711
I made the reservation.

13
00:01:47,796 --> 00:01:48,797
Soju or beer?

14
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:51,007
-[worker 2] Let's have both.
-[worker 3] Yeah, I don't know about that.

15
00:01:51,091 --> 00:01:52,300
[worker 4] Drink it all.

16
00:01:54,469 --> 00:01:56,346
[♪ pensive music playing]

17
00:01:57,764 --> 00:01:59,015
[door opens]

18
00:02:01,101 --> 00:02:02,644
[door closes]

19
00:02:03,270 --> 00:02:07,065
JI COMPUTER

20
00:02:18,076 --> 00:02:19,411
[Gyeongae] Good evening.

21
00:02:23,165 --> 00:02:24,374
[door unlocks]

22
00:02:25,834 --> 00:02:28,628
[door opens, closes]

23
00:02:29,796 --> 00:02:31,339
[keypad beeps]

24
00:02:35,552 --> 00:02:36,720
[sighs]

25
00:02:54,571 --> 00:02:55,822
[door chimes]

26
00:03:01,036 --> 00:03:02,454
[door chimes]

27
00:03:05,582 --> 00:03:07,083
[Gyeongae] Hello.

28
00:03:07,167 --> 00:03:08,835
Sir? Excuse me.

29
00:03:09,544 --> 00:03:11,254
-Just a minute. Hi.
-Oh, hi.

30
00:03:11,338 --> 00:03:12,756
[Gyeongae chuckles]

31
00:03:14,257 --> 00:03:15,926
-Hi, there.
-[whispers] Hi.

32
00:03:16,676 --> 00:03:18,261
Hey, wait. Hold on.

33
00:03:18,345 --> 00:03:20,639
-[sighs]
-We've been neighbors for a while now.

34
00:03:20,722 --> 00:03:24,935
I see you all the time, but I don't think
we've ever properly introduced ourselves.

35
00:03:25,602 --> 00:03:30,607
[chuckles] You see, I run a little
hair salon down the alley.

36
00:03:31,858 --> 00:03:33,360
Right next to the chicken place.

37
00:03:34,361 --> 00:03:35,529
[Manhui whispers] Right.

38
00:03:36,029 --> 00:03:38,490
-You know, down the alley…
-Yeah. Okay.

39
00:03:39,199 --> 00:03:41,034
Come by when you need a haircut.

40
00:03:41,117 --> 00:03:42,285
[whispers] Okay.

41
00:03:43,620 --> 00:03:45,539
Hey, I'm really sorry.

42
00:03:45,622 --> 00:03:48,500
Well, you look great now,

43
00:03:48,583 --> 00:03:51,545
but if you got
just a tiny little trim on your bangs,

44
00:03:51,628 --> 00:03:53,838
-you'd look so much better.
-[exhales]

45
00:03:54,422 --> 00:03:55,840
-Drop by sometime.
-Okay.
STYLE
::cue()

46
00:03:56,675 --> 00:03:58,426
Uh, wait, hold up.

47
00:03:59,010 --> 00:04:01,972
I don't think I can finish
all of this on my own.

48
00:04:02,055 --> 00:04:04,516
-Here, take this. Wait a minute.
-Okay.

49
00:04:04,599 --> 00:04:05,600
Oh, my gosh!

50
00:04:06,601 --> 00:04:07,727
Take this one instead.

51
00:04:07,811 --> 00:04:08,853
Hey, wait.

52
00:04:09,354 --> 00:04:10,939
[Gyeongae chuckles]

53
00:04:11,022 --> 00:04:13,191
Come by for a haircut sometime!

54
00:04:13,275 --> 00:04:14,317
Okay.

55
00:04:15,819 --> 00:04:17,487
He's cute. [chuckles]

56
00:04:24,452 --> 00:04:25,954
[sighs]

57
00:04:26,705 --> 00:04:29,791
[♪ emotional music playing]

58
00:04:32,502 --> 00:04:33,628
[sighs]

59
00:04:53,565 --> 00:04:54,608
[knocks on door]

60
00:04:54,691 --> 00:04:55,984
[visitor] Kim Gyeongae!

61
00:04:56,610 --> 00:04:57,819
Open up.

62
00:04:59,112 --> 00:05:00,363
I know you're in there.

63
00:05:01,323 --> 00:05:02,657
-Come on.
-[knocks on door]

64
00:05:03,742 --> 00:05:06,953
I know your lights were on until just now.
Open up while I'm being nice.

65
00:05:07,621 --> 00:05:09,539
[door unlocks]

66
00:05:09,623 --> 00:05:11,124
I'm not leaving empty-handed.

67
00:05:13,001 --> 00:05:14,085
Come out already!

68
00:05:14,878 --> 00:05:17,047
You better open up
before I kick the door down.

69
00:05:17,923 --> 00:05:20,383
Or I'm going to kill you.

70
00:05:22,093 --> 00:05:23,094
One.

71
00:05:23,637 --> 00:05:25,597
-Two!
-[door unlocks, chimes]

72
00:05:26,681 --> 00:05:29,267
-[breathing heavily]
-Look who it is. There you are.

73
00:05:29,809 --> 00:05:32,812
You can't just show up like this
in the middle of the night.

74
00:05:33,688 --> 00:05:36,024
[visitor] I know you made money today.
Hand it over.

75
00:05:36,107 --> 00:05:37,943
[Gyeongae] You just took all of it
a few days ago.

76
00:05:38,026 --> 00:05:39,361
I don't have any money right now.

77
00:05:39,444 --> 00:05:42,197
[visitor] If I find a single penny
in this dump, you're dead.

78
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:44,574
-[Gyeongae grunting]
-[slap]

79
00:05:44,658 --> 00:05:48,244
-I'm going to teach you a lesson!
-[Gyeongae grunting]

80
00:05:49,663 --> 00:05:52,624
-[Gyeongae panting, screaming]
-[objects thudding, clattering]

81
00:05:52,707 --> 00:05:54,542
-[visitor] Get your ass over here!
-[screaming continues]

82
00:05:54,626 --> 00:05:56,044
-Damn it.
-[panting]

83
00:05:56,127 --> 00:05:57,253
You think I'm kidding?

84
00:05:57,337 --> 00:05:59,297
-Stop it.
-[visitor] Look at me.

85
00:05:59,381 --> 00:06:02,676
[both grunting, groaning]

86
00:06:02,759 --> 00:06:03,885
Why don't you just…

87
00:06:04,594 --> 00:06:06,179
-Stop it, man.
-Get lost!

88
00:06:07,138 --> 00:06:08,807
Come here. You.

89
00:06:08,890 --> 00:06:11,142
What? You found yourself a guy already?

90
00:06:11,226 --> 00:06:13,687
Ha! Seriously, this is ridiculous.

91
00:06:14,187 --> 00:06:15,355
Come here.

92
00:06:15,939 --> 00:06:17,482
-[grunts]
-[grunts, screams]

93
00:06:17,565 --> 00:06:21,361
[visitor] So you've been giving
all that money to him?

94
00:06:21,444 --> 00:06:23,113
-Is that right? Come here.
-[Gyeongae grunting]

95
00:06:23,196 --> 00:06:26,282
[visitor] Come back here.
You don't have money to pay me,

96
00:06:26,366 --> 00:06:28,618
-but you've got money for him?
-[slapping]

97
00:06:30,537 --> 00:06:33,164
[visitor] So you've been busy
with your love life, huh?

98
00:06:33,707 --> 00:06:35,000
I said come here!

99
00:06:35,083 --> 00:06:36,793
-[grunts]
-[visitor groans]

100
00:06:38,044 --> 00:06:39,879
[panting]

101
00:06:41,297 --> 00:06:43,258
[breathing heavily]

102
00:06:43,341 --> 00:06:46,636
Wait. Hold on.

103
00:06:51,099 --> 00:06:52,642
I told you to stop it.

104
00:06:53,309 --> 00:06:54,769
[thud]

105
00:06:54,853 --> 00:06:58,148
I told you to stop it! [breathing heavily]

106
00:06:59,023 --> 00:07:02,193
I told you to stop.

107
00:07:02,277 --> 00:07:03,862
I told you, didn't I?

108
00:07:15,957 --> 00:07:17,625
[sighs]

109
00:07:23,256 --> 00:07:26,760
[panting]

110
00:07:33,141 --> 00:07:34,476
Uh…

111
00:07:34,559 --> 00:07:36,728
[panting continues]

112
00:07:40,356 --> 00:07:41,775
Uh…

113
00:07:42,609 --> 00:07:44,194
Uh…

114
00:07:47,280 --> 00:07:49,699
[panting continues]

115
00:07:51,284 --> 00:07:52,285
[grunts]
STYLE
::cue()

116
00:07:53,828 --> 00:07:55,038
What are you doing?

117
00:07:55,622 --> 00:07:57,248
I'm calling the cops.

118
00:07:57,332 --> 00:07:58,750
Hey, look at me.

119
00:08:00,293 --> 00:08:02,253
If you hadn't killed this man,

120
00:08:02,837 --> 00:08:04,714
I would've been dead.

121
00:08:08,259 --> 00:08:11,221
From now on, just do as I say.

122
00:08:11,930 --> 00:08:13,973
[breathes shakily]

123
00:08:17,769 --> 00:08:20,021
[♪ tense music playing]

124
00:08:58,768 --> 00:08:59,769
[chimes]

125
00:09:02,105 --> 00:09:03,690
[Gyeongae] Get inside.
You're getting rained on.

126
00:09:03,773 --> 00:09:05,150
Oh…

127
00:09:06,860 --> 00:09:08,695
[scrubbing]

128
00:09:15,535 --> 00:09:19,122
[Gyeongae humming]

129
00:09:51,905 --> 00:09:55,158
[snipping]

130
00:09:58,828 --> 00:10:00,079
It feels good, doesn't it?

131
00:10:06,336 --> 00:10:07,587
All done.

132
00:10:24,604 --> 00:10:27,106
[♪ mysterious music playing]

133
00:10:33,738 --> 00:10:35,990
[stammers] Well, thank you.

134
00:10:42,163 --> 00:10:43,498
For saving me.

135
00:10:53,424 --> 00:10:54,759
Thank you.

136
00:11:38,428 --> 00:11:43,349
THE HUSBAND
STYLE
::cue()

137
00:11:45,059 --> 00:11:48,229
[Taeju] It's a list of the top sponsors
of this hospital. Have a look.

138
00:11:49,188 --> 00:11:50,315
[heart monitor beeping]

139
00:11:50,398 --> 00:11:54,652
The other one's the list of people
who made it into the trial.

140
00:11:55,945 --> 00:11:57,655
The exact same names.

141
00:11:57,739 --> 00:12:00,575
LEE SEONGUK, PARK DOHYEON
OH MINSEOK

142
00:12:03,369 --> 00:12:05,288
It was all about money.

143
00:12:07,290 --> 00:12:10,835
You didn't lose your spot.
You just never had one to begin with.

144
00:12:13,713 --> 00:12:15,006
But…

145
00:12:16,591 --> 00:12:20,928
Then why did they tell me
it was because I'm an ex-con?

146
00:12:26,309 --> 00:12:27,435
Who said that?

147
00:12:28,770 --> 00:12:31,689
Who told you such a lie and why?

148
00:12:32,607 --> 00:12:35,193
[Dosik] The day Mr. Ha died,
you were in the same elevator.

149
00:12:35,777 --> 00:12:38,654
Plus, your recent contact
with Kim Gyeongae…

150
00:12:41,115 --> 00:12:42,492
Was this all a coincidence?

151
00:12:42,575 --> 00:12:44,660
-[♪ tense music playing]
-[sighs]

152
00:12:46,371 --> 00:12:47,455
Answer the question.

153
00:12:50,792 --> 00:12:52,794
When Ms. Kim Gyeongae was in prison,

154
00:12:54,170 --> 00:12:55,838
I handled her psychiatric treatment.

155
00:12:56,964 --> 00:13:00,426
I did it as a volunteer
before joining this hospital.

156
00:13:01,469 --> 00:13:03,679
I met her a few times after her release.

157
00:13:05,306 --> 00:13:07,934
I had meals with her
and checked in on her.

158
00:13:08,726 --> 00:13:10,353
She seemed like a decent person.

159
00:13:11,104 --> 00:13:13,856
I had no idea she'd go
and do something like this.

160
00:13:13,940 --> 00:13:15,149
That's all.

161
00:13:15,233 --> 00:13:17,235
-And that's why you kept this from us?
-Yes.

162
00:13:17,318 --> 00:13:19,070
I didn't want to get involved.

163
00:13:19,153 --> 00:13:23,324
When so many coincidences line up,
it means someone is lying.

164
00:13:23,408 --> 00:13:26,077
Then go find out who's lying.

165
00:13:28,621 --> 00:13:29,622
And next time,

166
00:13:30,873 --> 00:13:33,000
bring me evidence, not accusations.

167
00:13:33,084 --> 00:13:35,169
[phone buzzing]

168
00:13:38,089 --> 00:13:39,632
[sighs]

169
00:13:43,803 --> 00:13:44,804
Yeah.

170
00:13:45,304 --> 00:13:46,305
What?

171
00:13:47,181 --> 00:13:48,432
Right now?

172
00:13:48,516 --> 00:13:49,517
Got it.

173
00:13:50,768 --> 00:13:52,895
-[call ends]
-Let's continue another time.

174
00:13:52,979 --> 00:13:55,148
For now, get yourself to safety.

175
00:13:57,108 --> 00:13:59,152
Noh Manhui is on the way to the hospital.

176
00:13:59,235 --> 00:14:01,445
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

177
00:14:02,530 --> 00:14:04,574
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER

178
00:14:16,169 --> 00:14:18,462
[phone buzzes]

179
00:14:19,630 --> 00:14:20,923
Yeah, Detective Jang.

180
00:14:23,217 --> 00:14:24,260
What?

181
00:14:27,013 --> 00:14:28,389
[chimes]

182
00:14:30,224 --> 00:14:32,018
[phone buzzes]

183
00:14:33,519 --> 00:14:35,313
INCOMING CALL
HUSBAND

184
00:14:35,396 --> 00:14:38,441
-[tires screeching]
-[buzzing continues]

185
00:14:39,984 --> 00:14:42,028
[♪ dramatic music playing]

186
00:14:43,362 --> 00:14:44,655
[gasps]

187
00:14:45,781 --> 00:14:46,824
Ms. Ko.

188
00:14:46,908 --> 00:14:48,659
[buzzing continues]

189
00:14:48,743 --> 00:14:50,077
It's been a while.

190
00:14:52,038 --> 00:14:53,247
Where's Mr. Kang?

191
00:14:56,042 --> 00:14:57,168
MISSED CALL

192
00:14:57,251 --> 00:14:59,086
[♪ dramatic music continues]

193
00:14:59,170 --> 00:15:01,172
[breathing heavily]

194
00:15:04,675 --> 00:15:05,927
Don't move, okay?

195
00:15:06,010 --> 00:15:07,011
[foot tapping]

196
00:15:07,094 --> 00:15:08,471
[hyperventilating]

197
00:15:09,597 --> 00:15:10,848
I said don't move!

198
00:15:11,599 --> 00:15:13,809
[screams]

199
00:15:13,893 --> 00:15:15,978
[panting]

200
00:15:18,564 --> 00:15:20,691
[banging on door]

201
00:15:20,775 --> 00:15:23,069
[panting continues]

202
00:15:25,613 --> 00:15:28,074
[breathing heavily] I said don't move.

203
00:15:30,076 --> 00:15:31,535
[screams]

204
00:15:36,040 --> 00:15:37,041
Are you all right?

205
00:15:37,708 --> 00:15:39,126
Honey?

206
00:15:39,210 --> 00:15:40,253
[grunts]

207
00:15:40,336 --> 00:15:42,755
-[siren wailing]
-[panting]

208
00:15:48,177 --> 00:15:49,303
Stay right here.

209
00:15:49,387 --> 00:15:50,763
No! Don't go out there, honey!

210
00:15:50,846 --> 00:15:52,723
[siren continues]

211
00:16:01,983 --> 00:16:04,527
[♪ thrilling music playing]
STYLE
::cue()

212
00:16:40,021 --> 00:16:42,023
-[panting]
-[door unlocks]

213
00:16:42,940 --> 00:16:43,941
[Dosik] Ms. Ko!

214
00:16:44,942 --> 00:16:46,235
-Are you okay?
-Uh…

215
00:16:47,111 --> 00:16:48,529
[stammers] He went that way.

216
00:16:48,612 --> 00:16:50,031
-Go, get after him!
-On it.

217
00:16:50,114 --> 00:16:52,491
[siren continues]

218
00:16:52,575 --> 00:16:54,785
Send medical assistance
to the basement stairwell.

219
00:16:54,869 --> 00:16:57,204
[♪ thrilling music continues]

220
00:17:04,879 --> 00:17:06,088
[Gyeongae] Excuse me.

221
00:17:06,756 --> 00:17:07,757
Excuse me!

222
00:17:08,257 --> 00:17:10,301
Is something going on outside?

223
00:17:10,801 --> 00:17:12,595
[chains rattle]

224
00:17:13,095 --> 00:17:16,140
Excuse me!
I said, is something going on out there?

225
00:17:17,641 --> 00:17:19,310
Ms. Ko, take deep breaths.

226
00:17:20,603 --> 00:17:22,396
Hold on.

227
00:17:23,439 --> 00:17:24,440
What happened to her?

228
00:17:24,523 --> 00:17:27,610
We found her in the basement parking.
She's in severe hyperventilation.

229
00:17:27,693 --> 00:17:30,613
-[hyperventilating]
-I'll go with you. You're fine, Seyun.

230
00:17:30,696 --> 00:17:32,865
Just breathe. Slowly. Inhale…

231
00:17:36,994 --> 00:17:38,663
[horn honking]

232
00:17:39,955 --> 00:17:41,290
[horn honking]

233
00:17:43,584 --> 00:17:44,877
[horn honking]

234
00:17:48,422 --> 00:17:51,342
[♪ music intensifies]

235
00:18:23,541 --> 00:18:24,959
-[Taeju groans]
-[Manhui grunts]

236
00:18:27,294 --> 00:18:28,337
[grunts]

237
00:18:28,421 --> 00:18:29,714
[murmurs]

238
00:18:29,797 --> 00:18:31,340
[grunts]

239
00:18:36,512 --> 00:18:38,931
Hey, boss. Guess what?

240
00:18:40,349 --> 00:18:41,851
This is all your fault.

241
00:18:42,518 --> 00:18:44,103
-If you…
-[groans]

242
00:18:44,186 --> 00:18:46,147
…had just given me the money you promised,

243
00:18:46,230 --> 00:18:47,648
none of this would be happening.

244
00:18:47,732 --> 00:18:49,191
Who put you up to it?

245
00:18:49,942 --> 00:18:50,943
[grunts]

246
00:18:51,026 --> 00:18:52,027
Who…

247
00:18:53,529 --> 00:18:56,031
Who ordered you to kidnap my wife?

248
00:18:56,615 --> 00:18:57,658
[Manhui] Ah.

249
00:18:58,659 --> 00:19:00,286
That's what you want to know.

250
00:19:01,579 --> 00:19:02,621
That's too bad.

251
00:19:03,581 --> 00:19:05,833
You got it all wrong. [sighs]

252
00:19:07,001 --> 00:19:08,419
[grunts]

253
00:19:09,253 --> 00:19:10,755
Look, you got it all wrong.

254
00:19:10,838 --> 00:19:12,298
[panting]

255
00:19:12,381 --> 00:19:13,382
What?

256
00:19:15,301 --> 00:19:16,886
I wasn't after your wife.

257
00:19:20,514 --> 00:19:22,975
Hey, it was you.

258
00:19:24,059 --> 00:19:26,562
[♪ mysterious music playing]

259
00:19:26,645 --> 00:19:30,191
You're the one I was going to kill.

260
00:19:31,442 --> 00:19:33,068
What are you talking about?

261
00:19:33,778 --> 00:19:34,779
Me…

262
00:19:37,323 --> 00:19:41,035
On whose orders? And why?

263
00:19:43,078 --> 00:19:45,956
Does it really matter?
You're going to die either way.

264
00:19:51,504 --> 00:19:53,047
So will your wife.

265
00:19:54,298 --> 00:19:55,633
What?

266
00:19:55,716 --> 00:19:57,927
Your wife.

267
00:19:58,427 --> 00:20:01,096
They're going to kill her. [panting]

268
00:20:01,180 --> 00:20:03,098
They've already tried once.

269
00:20:03,891 --> 00:20:05,100
Someone tried to kill her?

270
00:20:05,810 --> 00:20:07,686
They ordered Dr. Ha Jeongsoo…

271
00:20:09,730 --> 00:20:11,524
to kill your wife.

272
00:20:14,693 --> 00:20:16,278
And how do you know that?

273
00:20:16,362 --> 00:20:18,155
Because I saved her.

274
00:20:18,823 --> 00:20:20,658
[panting continues]

275
00:20:27,456 --> 00:20:29,375
[groans]

276
00:20:30,251 --> 00:20:32,253
But they'll try to kill her again.

277
00:20:37,675 --> 00:20:41,136
[siren wailing]

278
00:20:49,854 --> 00:20:51,605
[pipe clatters]

279
00:20:54,984 --> 00:20:57,319
[siren continues]

280
00:21:02,199 --> 00:21:03,284
Thanks.

281
00:21:07,204 --> 00:21:09,164
It's a sedative.
You should feel better soon.

282
00:21:09,832 --> 00:21:11,250
[gasps]

283
00:21:13,002 --> 00:21:14,420
[sighs]

284
00:21:17,381 --> 00:21:18,799
[sighs]
STYLE
::cue()

285
00:21:22,469 --> 00:21:25,472
[siren wailing]

286
00:21:28,017 --> 00:21:30,978
LAW ENFORCEMENT

287
00:21:35,566 --> 00:21:37,192
Mr. Kang, are you okay?

288
00:21:37,943 --> 00:21:38,944
[Taeju] Yeah, I'm fine.

289
00:21:39,028 --> 00:21:41,739
You can't just go after him
by yourself like that.

290
00:21:43,699 --> 00:21:44,950
[sighs]

291
00:21:45,034 --> 00:21:50,539
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER

292
00:22:07,348 --> 00:22:09,350
Excuse me, nurse.
What's going on out there?

293
00:22:09,850 --> 00:22:11,810
-I'm here to change your IV bag.
-Yeah, okay,

294
00:22:11,894 --> 00:22:14,605
but is something going on outside?

295
00:22:14,688 --> 00:22:15,898
I'm talking to you.

296
00:22:15,981 --> 00:22:17,983
-Why won't you answer me?
-Please don't move.

297
00:22:18,943 --> 00:22:20,486
Your husband was here earlier.

298
00:22:21,570 --> 00:22:25,282
[♪ mysterious music playing]

299
00:22:38,170 --> 00:22:39,797
-[Taeju] Chiung.
-Hey.

300
00:22:40,381 --> 00:22:41,632
How's Seyun?

301
00:22:41,715 --> 00:22:43,258
Sedated for now.

302
00:22:43,342 --> 00:22:44,510
It's acute stress.

303
00:22:46,011 --> 00:22:49,348
Her body reacted since it was
similar to the trauma she suffered before.

304
00:22:50,516 --> 00:22:51,642
How are you holding up?

305
00:22:51,725 --> 00:22:52,768
Yeah, I'm fine.

306
00:22:53,352 --> 00:22:54,687
[inhales]

307
00:22:55,312 --> 00:22:56,605
Director Ko's inside.

308
00:22:58,190 --> 00:22:59,525
Oh, okay. Thanks a lot.

309
00:23:34,101 --> 00:23:35,477
[door closes]

310
00:23:37,980 --> 00:23:40,649
What did she do to deserve this?

311
00:23:41,692 --> 00:23:44,194
What are those damn cops doing?

312
00:23:45,571 --> 00:23:46,572
What?

313
00:23:46,655 --> 00:23:48,907
You still suspect me?

314
00:23:48,991 --> 00:23:51,535
You still think I tried to have
my own daughter kidnapped

315
00:23:51,618 --> 00:23:53,328
and that woman killed?

316
00:23:54,371 --> 00:23:59,043
I don't even want to imagine
that you'd do such a thing to Seyun.

317
00:23:59,126 --> 00:24:00,419
So…

318
00:24:01,545 --> 00:24:03,714
let's be honest with each other.

319
00:24:03,797 --> 00:24:07,426
I can't just stand by
and watch Seyun face danger anymore.

320
00:24:08,510 --> 00:24:09,595
Kim Gyeongae…

321
00:24:12,222 --> 00:24:13,807
You knew about her, didn't you?

322
00:24:15,434 --> 00:24:16,685
[sighs]

323
00:24:16,769 --> 00:24:19,563
Yes, I've seen her before.

324
00:24:20,773 --> 00:24:24,526
I met her when she came in to apply,

325
00:24:24,610 --> 00:24:26,195
with that damn husband of hers.

326
00:24:26,945 --> 00:24:28,030
Kim Gyeongae…

327
00:24:29,573 --> 00:24:31,909
I heard she was screened out
because she's an ex-con.

328
00:24:31,992 --> 00:24:33,535
Is that true?

329
00:24:35,079 --> 00:24:36,371
Who on earth told you that?

330
00:24:36,455 --> 00:24:37,956
Am I wrong?

331
00:24:38,040 --> 00:24:40,375
How the hell would I know
if that woman's an ex-con?

332
00:24:41,085 --> 00:24:43,170
That's not on her application.

333
00:24:44,630 --> 00:24:46,882
So she dared to kidnap my daughter

334
00:24:47,466 --> 00:24:49,968
because she wasn't selected
for my project?

335
00:24:52,054 --> 00:24:53,138
I see.

336
00:24:54,056 --> 00:24:55,182
But you know,

337
00:24:56,517 --> 00:24:59,269
that might actually be where it all began.

338
00:25:01,063 --> 00:25:02,147
What?

339
00:25:03,190 --> 00:25:05,275
Because it wasn't fair.

340
00:25:06,819 --> 00:25:09,988
You went on about hope and excitement.

341
00:25:10,864 --> 00:25:13,867
And who gets to enjoy them
all came down to money, didn't it?

342
00:25:14,493 --> 00:25:16,578
That's not how I see it.

343
00:25:17,079 --> 00:25:19,289
Donations fund our research,

344
00:25:19,915 --> 00:25:21,583
which saves future patients.

345
00:25:22,501 --> 00:25:25,921
That woman was denied
the opportunity to save her own life.

346
00:25:27,047 --> 00:25:29,174
We can't save every patient.

347
00:25:30,467 --> 00:25:32,386
I opted for the best option…

348
00:25:34,221 --> 00:25:36,223
for a better future.

349
00:25:38,767 --> 00:25:39,768
And I know…

350
00:25:41,728 --> 00:25:43,355
my decision was the right one.

351
00:25:43,438 --> 00:25:46,316
It's that greed of yours
that dragged us into this mess.

352
00:25:46,400 --> 00:25:47,818
I hope you know that.

353
00:25:52,156 --> 00:25:53,157
Father.

354
00:25:55,075 --> 00:25:58,412
Besides you, me, and Dr. Ha,
STYLE
::cue()

355
00:25:59,788 --> 00:26:02,875
who else knows about the hospital

356
00:26:03,917 --> 00:26:05,252
using fetal stem cell samples?

357
00:26:23,687 --> 00:26:25,939
[beeps]

358
00:26:26,023 --> 00:26:28,942
[luggage thudding]

359
00:26:34,615 --> 00:26:37,159
[phone buzzing]

360
00:26:37,910 --> 00:26:39,578
SEONGJIN POLICE
DETECTIVE JANG DOSIK

361
00:26:39,661 --> 00:26:42,331
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

362
00:26:43,874 --> 00:26:45,334
[car beeps]

363
00:26:58,222 --> 00:26:59,431
Long time no see.

364
00:26:59,932 --> 00:27:00,933
How have you been?

365
00:27:06,521 --> 00:27:08,482
But where are you off to in such a hurry,

366
00:27:09,733 --> 00:27:10,734
Dr. Cha Myeonghui?

367
00:27:16,740 --> 00:27:20,160
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER

368
00:27:34,257 --> 00:27:36,718
[sighs]

369
00:27:51,066 --> 00:27:52,651
[knocks on door]

370
00:27:52,734 --> 00:27:54,486
-Yes?
-[door opens]

371
00:27:58,198 --> 00:27:59,241
Are you doing okay?

372
00:28:02,077 --> 00:28:03,495
You need to take it easy.

373
00:28:03,578 --> 00:28:04,788
[door closes]

374
00:28:07,165 --> 00:28:08,709
You look worse than I do.

375
00:28:13,380 --> 00:28:16,008
You shouldn't have gone
after him like that. He's dangerous.

376
00:28:20,012 --> 00:28:22,973
Well, you're
not the type to listen, anyway.

377
00:28:33,316 --> 00:28:35,027
Anything else you want to tell me?

378
00:28:38,071 --> 00:28:39,156
Yeah, there is.

379
00:28:44,828 --> 00:28:45,829
What is it?

380
00:28:46,455 --> 00:28:48,915
I thought it was about time you knew.

381
00:28:50,792 --> 00:28:52,502
About our spinal cord project.

382
00:28:54,254 --> 00:28:56,089
It was problematic from the beginning.

383
00:28:58,216 --> 00:28:59,509
What do you mean?

384
00:29:00,135 --> 00:29:02,637
The selection for the clinical trial…

385
00:29:03,805 --> 00:29:05,265
It wasn't made fairly.

386
00:29:06,808 --> 00:29:10,437
The spots were reserved
for the top donors from the get-go.

387
00:29:10,520 --> 00:29:11,521
What?

388
00:29:12,939 --> 00:29:14,274
What are you talking about?

389
00:29:14,900 --> 00:29:18,070
The stem cells we were using in
our procedures weren't the approved ones.

390
00:29:18,945 --> 00:29:21,281
They were illegally sourced
fetal stem cells.

391
00:29:24,367 --> 00:29:25,494
[exhales]

392
00:29:26,161 --> 00:29:27,496
There's no way.

393
00:29:32,626 --> 00:29:34,669
Who made those decisions?

394
00:29:40,175 --> 00:29:42,844
You see, I thought your father

395
00:29:43,929 --> 00:29:46,431
had something to do with this.

396
00:29:47,516 --> 00:29:49,893
That's why I asked you
to look for those files.

397
00:29:53,897 --> 00:29:57,359
Kim Gyeongae was one
of the applicants who didn't make the cut.

398
00:29:58,735 --> 00:30:00,695
She never stood a chance to begin with.

399
00:30:02,864 --> 00:30:05,283
So is that why all of this is happening?

400
00:30:06,910 --> 00:30:08,411
Because of my dad?

401
00:30:11,414 --> 00:30:14,251
It's true that your father
made his share of mistakes,

402
00:30:14,334 --> 00:30:18,130
but he wasn't behind your kidnapping.
I've confirmed that myself.

403
00:30:19,589 --> 00:30:21,133
[scoffs]

404
00:30:23,260 --> 00:30:25,762
[♪ intriguing music playing]

405
00:30:30,142 --> 00:30:32,269
[door opens, closes]
STYLE
::cue()

406
00:30:35,147 --> 00:30:36,523
[sighs]

407
00:30:43,071 --> 00:30:44,573
Did you get any sleep last night?

408
00:30:45,240 --> 00:30:46,533
[scoffs]

409
00:30:46,616 --> 00:30:49,661
What about you?
It looked like you didn't sleep a wink.

410
00:30:51,621 --> 00:30:52,998
[sighing] Gosh.

411
00:30:54,040 --> 00:30:55,167
Stop worrying so much.

412
00:30:56,418 --> 00:30:59,713
I've been checking in on Seyun at work,

413
00:31:00,380 --> 00:31:02,090
and Taeju is with her.

414
00:31:02,716 --> 00:31:03,717
You're right.

415
00:31:05,510 --> 00:31:08,263
You have to stay strong
at times like this. [chuckles]

416
00:31:08,889 --> 00:31:10,557
HAIR COLLAGEN 3270

417
00:31:12,893 --> 00:31:13,894
Gosh.

418
00:31:14,519 --> 00:31:17,606
I've been so out of it
that I completely forgot to take this.

419
00:31:17,689 --> 00:31:21,193
No patient wants a hospital director
who looks more washed out than they do.

420
00:31:21,276 --> 00:31:23,236
Take one every day. Don't forget.

421
00:31:23,320 --> 00:31:24,446
[chuckles]

422
00:31:25,280 --> 00:31:29,868
You know, I've noticed
that taking this makes a big difference.

423
00:31:29,951 --> 00:31:31,328
[both chuckle]

424
00:31:32,954 --> 00:31:34,915
It's also supposed
to be good for your skin.

425
00:31:34,998 --> 00:31:36,583
You should take one too.

426
00:31:36,666 --> 00:31:38,376
-Shall I?
-Mmm.

427
00:31:45,050 --> 00:31:46,468
[sighs]

428
00:31:46,968 --> 00:31:48,970
It already feels good. [chuckles]

429
00:31:50,138 --> 00:31:51,514
Things will get better in time.

430
00:31:52,974 --> 00:31:54,351
I hope so.

431
00:32:02,150 --> 00:32:03,860
[chattering]

432
00:32:11,493 --> 00:32:13,912
Oh, Dr. Kang.
Are you hurt at all from yesterday?

433
00:32:14,496 --> 00:32:17,165
-No, I'm fine. But what's going on?
-[Dosik sighs]

434
00:32:17,832 --> 00:32:19,501
Ms. Cha Myeonghui has fled.

435
00:32:20,252 --> 00:32:21,836
What do you mean, she's fled?

436
00:32:21,920 --> 00:32:24,422
You see, she was the last person
Mr. Ha was with

437
00:32:24,506 --> 00:32:26,883
on the day he died,
which makes her a prime suspect.

438
00:32:27,842 --> 00:32:28,843
Myeonghui?

439
00:32:28,927 --> 00:32:31,346
She's known Kim Gyeongae
since she was in prison.

440
00:32:31,429 --> 00:32:34,516
It seems like they've been
in touch after her release too.

441
00:32:35,183 --> 00:32:37,060
Myeonghui was acquainted

442
00:32:37,978 --> 00:32:40,480
with Kim Gyeongae?

443
00:32:40,563 --> 00:32:43,733
Yes, we went to her house
with an arrest warrant,

444
00:32:44,317 --> 00:32:46,861
but she'd already packed up
and disappeared.

445
00:33:24,774 --> 00:33:26,067
BEHAVIORAL HEALTH
CONSULTATION ROOM

446
00:33:26,151 --> 00:33:27,152
[knocks on door]

447
00:33:35,493 --> 00:33:36,911
Come on in, Taeju.

448
00:33:46,963 --> 00:33:48,089
Are you okay?

449
00:33:50,216 --> 00:33:51,217
No.

450
00:33:54,971 --> 00:33:56,264
[sighs]

451
00:33:56,348 --> 00:33:59,059
Sounds like the talk didn't go so well.
STYLE
::cue()

452
00:34:01,353 --> 00:34:02,687
[sighs]

453
00:34:04,230 --> 00:34:07,108
I thought we'd been using
adult stem cells.

454
00:34:09,152 --> 00:34:10,403
But we weren't.

455
00:34:13,031 --> 00:34:14,866
They were fetal stem cells.

456
00:34:16,451 --> 00:34:18,286
Fetal stem cells?

457
00:34:20,205 --> 00:34:21,206
Yes.

458
00:34:22,332 --> 00:34:24,167
So that's what it was.

459
00:34:26,252 --> 00:34:27,253
Have you

460
00:34:28,004 --> 00:34:29,547
told anyone else about it?

461
00:34:32,384 --> 00:34:33,426
No, not yet.

462
00:34:35,595 --> 00:34:37,514
Sorry for showing up out of the blue.

463
00:34:37,597 --> 00:34:40,433
I had nowhere else
to sort my thoughts out.

464
00:34:41,851 --> 00:34:42,936
No, it's good.

465
00:34:43,645 --> 00:34:44,896
I'm glad you came.

466
00:34:46,606 --> 00:34:48,608
I should tell Seyun, shouldn't I?

467
00:34:50,693 --> 00:34:51,694
Taeju.

468
00:34:54,155 --> 00:34:55,281
Uh…

469
00:34:57,534 --> 00:34:59,953
You're still processing this right now.

470
00:35:01,162 --> 00:35:02,747
Do you think Seyun would be

471
00:35:03,665 --> 00:35:06,751
able to handle this if you told her now?

472
00:35:08,294 --> 00:35:09,838
It'll just cause misunderstandings.

473
00:35:11,673 --> 00:35:14,175
You may not have known about it,
but you've been using

474
00:35:15,510 --> 00:35:18,638
illegal material in your procedures.
That much is true.

475
00:35:21,850 --> 00:35:23,184
[sighs]

476
00:35:26,980 --> 00:35:28,898
It's okay. It happens.

477
00:35:35,113 --> 00:35:36,489
It's okay, Taeju.

478
00:35:39,868 --> 00:35:41,035
Don't you worry.

479
00:35:41,911 --> 00:35:43,163
This isn't the end.

480
00:35:45,039 --> 00:35:46,124
[inhales]

481
00:35:46,207 --> 00:35:47,250
I should be going.

482
00:35:50,336 --> 00:35:52,005
Thank you for hearing me out.

483
00:35:53,381 --> 00:35:54,841
Taeju.

484
00:35:58,386 --> 00:36:00,263
Now's not the time.

485
00:36:00,346 --> 00:36:01,556
You must not tell her.

486
00:36:02,307 --> 00:36:04,225
[♪ tense music playing]

487
00:36:07,270 --> 00:36:08,438
Never.

488
00:36:11,733 --> 00:36:13,651
[Taeju] She knew all about it,

489
00:36:13,735 --> 00:36:15,320
even before I told her.

490
00:36:40,220 --> 00:36:43,890
Honestly, every time I saw you people,
I kept thinking, "Why would they do this?"

491
00:36:43,973 --> 00:36:45,558
"Just why?"

492
00:36:47,811 --> 00:36:51,022
"Why did they do this to my wife?
Why did they kidnap her?"

493
00:36:57,695 --> 00:37:00,281
But to find out
that you were after me, not my wife…

494
00:37:01,574 --> 00:37:02,700
That was kind of a shock.

495
00:37:06,162 --> 00:37:08,665
How do you know that? Who told you?

496
00:37:09,374 --> 00:37:10,500
Noh Manhui.

497
00:37:11,292 --> 00:37:12,710
Your husband, Noh Manhui.

498
00:37:14,462 --> 00:37:16,673
You met my husband?

499
00:37:16,756 --> 00:37:19,801
He seemed quite shocked
when I told him Dr. Ha tried to kill you.

500
00:37:19,884 --> 00:37:21,970
He was very worried about you.

501
00:37:23,304 --> 00:37:24,305
So now…

502
00:37:26,307 --> 00:37:27,767
your husband should know as well.
STYLE
::cue()

503
00:37:30,353 --> 00:37:32,856
That you were both used and tossed aside.

504
00:37:38,027 --> 00:37:42,448
Right before he died,
Dr. Ha met Myeonghui in the elevator.

505
00:37:42,532 --> 00:37:44,367
After they talked,

506
00:37:44,450 --> 00:37:47,787
he changed his destination,
and died moments later.

507
00:37:49,831 --> 00:37:53,001
Dr. Cha was there with him?

508
00:37:53,084 --> 00:37:54,085
Why?

509
00:37:54,168 --> 00:37:57,255
Why are you so surprised
that those two ran into each other?

510
00:38:01,718 --> 00:38:03,803
I've been thinking about it.

511
00:38:06,598 --> 00:38:08,099
Myeonghui was in the know as well.

512
00:38:08,850 --> 00:38:09,851
About what?

513
00:38:11,603 --> 00:38:13,688
The fetal stem cells.

514
00:38:18,610 --> 00:38:20,028
Was it Dr. Cha?

515
00:38:22,238 --> 00:38:24,949
The one who lied to you
that your prior got you rejected?

516
00:38:27,160 --> 00:38:29,954
I mean, you two
have been in touch all along,

517
00:38:30,038 --> 00:38:31,915
since back when you were in prison.

518
00:38:33,207 --> 00:38:36,794
Yeah, so what?
I mean, what's so wrong about that?

519
00:38:39,130 --> 00:38:40,465
Ah.

520
00:38:41,299 --> 00:38:42,967
You must think

521
00:38:43,927 --> 00:38:46,971
you're in a different league
than a criminal like me, don't you?

522
00:38:48,056 --> 00:38:49,682
But guess what?

523
00:38:50,475 --> 00:38:54,938
You're the one who exploited
those dead babies

524
00:38:55,021 --> 00:38:57,148
for your benefit, not me.

525
00:38:59,567 --> 00:39:00,735
All I wanted…

526
00:39:01,694 --> 00:39:02,737
I…

527
00:39:02,820 --> 00:39:04,447
I just wanted to live.

528
00:39:07,241 --> 00:39:08,910
It can't be Dr. Cha.

529
00:39:10,244 --> 00:39:13,539
She always told me to never give up.

530
00:39:14,040 --> 00:39:16,000
She said in that clinical trial,

531
00:39:16,084 --> 00:39:20,546
they could make brand-new nerves
and put them into me.

532
00:39:21,130 --> 00:39:22,215
She said she'd help me.

533
00:39:22,840 --> 00:39:26,260
She told you that
they'd give you new nerves?

534
00:39:28,554 --> 00:39:31,182
Dr. Cha said that to you?
She's a psychiatrist.

535
00:39:33,559 --> 00:39:38,231
I mean, how could she possibly
help you in that situation?

536
00:39:41,651 --> 00:39:42,986
Myeonghui…

537
00:39:47,615 --> 00:39:50,618
introduced you to someone, didn't she?

538
00:39:53,287 --> 00:39:56,708
I don't even know
what you're talking about.

539
00:39:56,791 --> 00:39:58,084
What are you even saying?

540
00:39:59,961 --> 00:40:02,964
She's gone off the grid.
What was she so afraid of?

541
00:40:04,590 --> 00:40:08,845
Your husband ran away, Dr. Ha is dead,
and Myeonghui's disappeared.

542
00:40:11,347 --> 00:40:12,432
So now…

543
00:40:14,726 --> 00:40:16,185
you're all by yourself.

544
00:40:24,736 --> 00:40:27,280
-[door closes]
-They're all the same.

545
00:40:27,363 --> 00:40:30,033
They all use me and just toss me aside.

546
00:40:34,203 --> 00:40:37,206
WING 102 ROOM 07
KIM G.A
STYLE
::cue()

547
00:41:18,456 --> 00:41:20,708
FUND DONATION AGREEMENT,
CLINICAL TRIAL APPLICATION

548
00:41:22,168 --> 00:41:23,336
DONATION: 100 MILLION WON

549
00:41:23,419 --> 00:41:26,130
APPLICANT NAME: OH MINSEOK
STATUS: ACCEPTED

550
00:41:27,423 --> 00:41:28,508
DONATION: 550 MILLION WON

551
00:41:28,591 --> 00:41:30,885
APPLICANT NAME: LEE SEONGUK
STATUS: ACCEPTED

552
00:41:30,968 --> 00:41:32,011
[gasps]

553
00:41:32,553 --> 00:41:33,554
DONATION: 270 MILLION WON

554
00:41:34,472 --> 00:41:36,933
APPLICANT NAME: PARK DOHYEON
STATUS: ACCEPTED

555
00:41:38,810 --> 00:41:40,603
KIM JEONGHUI
DONATION: 190 MILLION WON

556
00:41:47,360 --> 00:41:50,947
APPLICANT NAME: KIM GYEONGAE
STATUS: SCREENED OUT

557
00:41:51,030 --> 00:41:52,949
STATUS: SCREENED OUT

558
00:41:54,700 --> 00:41:56,077
[Seyun's mother] What are you doing here?

559
00:42:01,833 --> 00:42:04,252
Why are you in your father's study?

560
00:42:06,629 --> 00:42:08,131
Mom, did you know about this?

561
00:42:09,215 --> 00:42:10,883
About what, dear?

562
00:42:12,426 --> 00:42:13,928
About what Dad did.

563
00:42:15,346 --> 00:42:17,974
[chuckles] What are you talking about?

564
00:42:21,519 --> 00:42:23,855
Never mind. It's nothing.
Don't worry about it.

565
00:42:26,524 --> 00:42:27,859
Wait, Seyun?

566
00:42:40,496 --> 00:42:41,831
Seyun.

567
00:42:51,507 --> 00:42:54,343
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER
FUND DONATION AGREEMENT

568
00:43:00,558 --> 00:43:02,560
It was just as you said.

569
00:43:04,478 --> 00:43:06,063
Why didn't you tell me?

570
00:43:07,690 --> 00:43:09,525
Do I not deserve to know?

571
00:43:16,032 --> 00:43:18,451
I had no idea what my dad had done.

572
00:43:21,204 --> 00:43:23,206
But you knew all along.

573
00:43:24,457 --> 00:43:26,125
Why did you make me out to be a fool?

574
00:43:27,418 --> 00:43:29,003
It's not like that, Seyun.

575
00:43:30,171 --> 00:43:31,172
Then what is it?

576
00:43:35,801 --> 00:43:37,511
I just felt like I shouldn't tell you.

577
00:43:38,387 --> 00:43:39,388
Why not?

578
00:43:43,226 --> 00:43:44,977
Why did you think you shouldn't tell me?

579
00:43:45,561 --> 00:43:46,562
Why?

580
00:43:52,360 --> 00:43:53,736
[gasps]

581
00:43:56,447 --> 00:43:57,490
Hold on.

582
00:43:58,199 --> 00:43:59,450
[gasps]

583
00:44:00,201 --> 00:44:01,369
That day…

584
00:44:02,995 --> 00:44:04,413
The day we lost Hayun.

585
00:44:05,373 --> 00:44:06,958
Were you late because…

586
00:44:08,542 --> 00:44:10,336
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

587
00:44:11,254 --> 00:44:15,007
The patients consented to the procedure
thinking it was their own stem cells.

588
00:44:15,800 --> 00:44:17,802
This is completely illegal, Father.

589
00:44:17,885 --> 00:44:19,804
Those illegal procedures

590
00:44:20,680 --> 00:44:23,766
helped people regain movement
and stand on their own two feet.

591
00:44:24,809 --> 00:44:27,687
They're hopeful
and excited about the future.

592
00:44:28,771 --> 00:44:30,314
That is not hope.

593
00:44:33,276 --> 00:44:36,862
Any hope that's built on a lie
is bound to fall apart.

594
00:44:38,114 --> 00:44:40,116
Please count me out of this project.
STYLE
::cue()

595
00:44:46,831 --> 00:44:48,165
What about Seyun?

596
00:44:51,002 --> 00:44:52,586
What will you do about her?

597
00:44:53,796 --> 00:44:55,464
Whether you do the surgery or not,

598
00:44:56,340 --> 00:44:57,800
that's your call.

599
00:44:59,385 --> 00:45:02,138
But it won't be you

600
00:45:03,139 --> 00:45:04,390
who pays the price.

601
00:45:05,266 --> 00:45:06,851
It will be Seyun.

602
00:45:10,771 --> 00:45:11,981
[sighs]

603
00:45:17,570 --> 00:45:18,654
Dr. Kang.

604
00:45:20,906 --> 00:45:22,325
I mean, Taeju.

605
00:45:23,451 --> 00:45:25,202
Do you think I've never felt that way?

606
00:45:26,537 --> 00:45:28,039
I've been there.

607
00:45:28,122 --> 00:45:31,083
But I had a family to protect.

608
00:45:31,167 --> 00:45:33,336
I just had to suck it up.

609
00:45:33,919 --> 00:45:36,756
That's how I've kept myself going.

610
00:45:41,218 --> 00:45:42,553
Your heart,

611
00:45:43,596 --> 00:45:44,930
your values, your morals…

612
00:45:45,431 --> 00:45:46,974
Just put them all aside.

613
00:45:48,476 --> 00:45:50,394
Don't let Seyun catch on.

614
00:45:50,978 --> 00:45:53,689
It'd only hurt her, all right?

615
00:45:54,732 --> 00:45:55,858
If you

616
00:45:57,276 --> 00:46:00,613
really love her, please.

617
00:46:46,117 --> 00:46:47,284
You're home.

618
00:46:49,412 --> 00:46:51,330
Where were you all night?

619
00:46:52,206 --> 00:46:53,833
Why are you out here?

620
00:46:53,916 --> 00:46:55,418
You should be in bed.

621
00:46:57,002 --> 00:46:59,046
You've been acting weird lately.

622
00:46:59,130 --> 00:47:01,215
You're always late,
and I can never reach you.

623
00:47:05,553 --> 00:47:06,720
Something came up.

624
00:47:07,388 --> 00:47:08,597
[sighs]

625
00:47:11,434 --> 00:47:12,768
Honey.

626
00:47:14,228 --> 00:47:15,813
Are you hiding something from me?

627
00:47:18,441 --> 00:47:19,608
I'm not.

628
00:47:22,736 --> 00:47:24,321
You sure there's nothing going on?

629
00:47:26,073 --> 00:47:27,074
I'm sure.

630
00:47:29,618 --> 00:47:31,036
Fine.

631
00:47:33,998 --> 00:47:35,332
Listen.

632
00:47:36,083 --> 00:47:37,418
I'm your wife.

633
00:47:38,878 --> 00:47:42,631
You have to tell me
if there is something going on.

634
00:47:43,299 --> 00:47:46,844
I can tell you're having a hard time,
but you won't say anything.

635
00:47:51,182 --> 00:47:52,308
[sighs]

636
00:47:59,690 --> 00:48:01,025
Where's your wedding ring?

637
00:48:03,152 --> 00:48:06,530
I took it off before surgery.
I probably left it in the office.

638
00:48:10,618 --> 00:48:12,620
-I'm going to turn in.
-All right.

639
00:48:14,914 --> 00:48:19,960
[door opens, closes]

640
00:48:20,044 --> 00:48:21,712
Daddy.

641
00:48:22,505 --> 00:48:23,589
Oh, hey, Hayun.

642
00:48:23,672 --> 00:48:25,132
My goodness.

643
00:48:25,216 --> 00:48:27,343
What are you doing up so late?

644
00:48:27,426 --> 00:48:28,928
Waiting for you, Daddy.

645
00:48:29,011 --> 00:48:30,930
Goodness, did you?

646
00:48:31,013 --> 00:48:33,224
My sweet little girl.

647
00:48:36,810 --> 00:48:38,437
[♪ intriguing music playing]
STYLE
::cue()

648
00:48:42,441 --> 00:48:43,984
HOSPITAL DIRECTOR'S OFFICE

649
00:48:44,068 --> 00:48:45,236
[Dr. Ko] Your heart…

650
00:48:46,654 --> 00:48:48,197
Just put them all aside.

651
00:48:49,198 --> 00:48:52,743
If you really love her, please.

652
00:48:54,995 --> 00:48:56,121
[knocks on door]

653
00:48:56,705 --> 00:48:59,667
-[life support beeping]
-[heart monitor beeping]

654
00:49:13,973 --> 00:49:16,684
[♪ music intensifies]

655
00:49:42,585 --> 00:49:46,171
Dr. Ko, your granddaughter has
just been brought into the ER.

656
00:49:46,255 --> 00:49:48,591
-What? Hayun is here?
-Yes.

657
00:49:48,674 --> 00:49:50,009
How bad is it?

658
00:49:50,676 --> 00:49:52,720
It looks like she has
a cervical spine injury.

659
00:49:52,803 --> 00:49:54,221
She needs emergency surgery.

660
00:49:54,722 --> 00:49:57,600
Ms. Ko is looking for Dr. Kang.

661
00:49:58,392 --> 00:50:00,352
Should I give him a call?

662
00:50:04,064 --> 00:50:05,065
[nurse] Dr. Ko?

663
00:50:06,734 --> 00:50:08,444
He's connecting nerve ends right now.

664
00:50:09,445 --> 00:50:12,615
If he stops now,
the patient will never stand again.

665
00:50:14,450 --> 00:50:16,535
Tell Dr. Park to take over
the surgery for now.

666
00:50:17,411 --> 00:50:21,081
I'll talk to Dr. Kang
when he's done with this.

667
00:50:24,209 --> 00:50:25,544
Wait, Doctor.

668
00:50:25,628 --> 00:50:27,838
Can you wait until Dr. Kang gets here?

669
00:50:28,505 --> 00:50:29,757
We don't have time.

670
00:50:29,840 --> 00:50:31,008
We'll try our best.

671
00:50:31,091 --> 00:50:33,177
Ms. Ko. I have to ask you
to wait out here.

672
00:50:33,260 --> 00:50:34,845
CALLING
HUSBAND

673
00:50:34,928 --> 00:50:36,305
[line ringing]

674
00:50:36,388 --> 00:50:38,724
Come on, honey, pick up.

675
00:50:38,807 --> 00:50:40,934
Please. Hayun is…

676
00:50:42,603 --> 00:50:46,148
-[line disconnected]
-Where is he? Why won't he pick up?

677
00:50:46,231 --> 00:50:47,608
-[line ringing]
-[breathing heavily]

678
00:50:47,691 --> 00:50:49,360
Where on earth is he?

679
00:50:50,110 --> 00:50:51,737
Okay, can you wrap this up for me?

680
00:50:51,820 --> 00:50:52,905
-Okay.
-Okay.

681
00:51:11,340 --> 00:51:12,591
[beeping]

682
00:51:12,675 --> 00:51:13,676
[doctor] She's flatlining!

683
00:51:13,759 --> 00:51:16,428
[heart monitor flatlining]

684
00:51:32,486 --> 00:51:33,570
[doctor] Dr. Kang.

685
00:51:35,364 --> 00:51:37,324
[sobbing]

686
00:51:43,330 --> 00:51:44,998
Where have you been?

687
00:51:49,837 --> 00:51:52,172
[sobbing continues]

688
00:51:58,929 --> 00:52:02,307
I said, where have you been?

689
00:52:07,813 --> 00:52:08,939
[sniffles]
STYLE
::cue()

690
00:52:09,022 --> 00:52:11,024
Where have you been?

691
00:52:12,860 --> 00:52:14,778
[♪ emotional music playing]

692
00:52:15,404 --> 00:52:18,240
[sobbing] Answer me!

693
00:52:22,202 --> 00:52:23,537
Why?

694
00:52:27,207 --> 00:52:30,127
Why have you carried
that burden all by yourself?

695
00:52:34,173 --> 00:52:36,049
I had no idea,

696
00:52:37,092 --> 00:52:39,011
so I just kept blaming you.

697
00:52:39,678 --> 00:52:40,971
Asking where you were,

698
00:52:41,054 --> 00:52:43,766
why you never came,
and saying it was all your fault.

699
00:52:49,438 --> 00:52:50,606
[sighs]

700
00:52:57,446 --> 00:53:00,949
It must've been just as hard on you
after we lost Hayun.

701
00:53:03,243 --> 00:53:05,662
Why you had changed so much

702
00:53:05,746 --> 00:53:07,831
and why you'd become so silent…

703
00:53:09,124 --> 00:53:10,959
I didn't even try to understand.

704
00:53:11,835 --> 00:53:13,879
I just kept pushing you
to answer my questions,

705
00:53:14,671 --> 00:53:16,840
without ever trying to hear you out.

706
00:53:18,967 --> 00:53:20,344
[gasps]

707
00:53:22,471 --> 00:53:24,681
You should've told me.

708
00:53:24,765 --> 00:53:26,975
Why couldn't you just tell me?

709
00:53:27,893 --> 00:53:30,938
I had no idea,
so all I could do was resent you.

710
00:53:33,816 --> 00:53:35,234
I was afraid…

711
00:53:38,862 --> 00:53:40,364
that you'd break down.

712
00:53:42,407 --> 00:53:43,408
What?

713
00:53:46,370 --> 00:53:50,958
Hayun is already gone, and I thought
the truth would push you over the edge.

714
00:53:54,336 --> 00:53:55,337
That's

715
00:53:57,130 --> 00:53:58,131
what I was…

716
00:54:01,218 --> 00:54:02,719
so scared of.

717
00:54:12,771 --> 00:54:14,815
I'm okay with you resenting me.

718
00:54:14,898 --> 00:54:16,608
Even if you resented me and blamed me,

719
00:54:17,693 --> 00:54:19,528
I'd stay by your side.

720
00:54:21,280 --> 00:54:22,281
But…

721
00:54:23,490 --> 00:54:27,911
if you found out the truth
and broke down, I…

722
00:54:30,706 --> 00:54:31,874
I thought if that happened, I…

723
00:54:36,044 --> 00:54:37,671
I might lose you too.

724
00:54:39,089 --> 00:54:41,174
I was so scared of that.

725
00:54:41,258 --> 00:54:42,259
I'm sorry.

726
00:54:42,885 --> 00:54:44,303
[sighs]

727
00:54:46,847 --> 00:54:49,308
[sobs] I'm sorry.

728
00:54:52,811 --> 00:54:54,354
I'm so sorry, honey.

729
00:54:58,567 --> 00:55:02,029
It must have been so hard.

730
00:55:02,821 --> 00:55:05,991
You must've been living in hell, honey.

731
00:55:08,076 --> 00:55:09,077
No.

732
00:55:09,870 --> 00:55:11,204
I'm sorry.

733
00:55:11,747 --> 00:55:13,081
I'm so sorry.

734
00:55:13,165 --> 00:55:16,418
I'm sorry, honey.
You can tell me anything now, okay?

735
00:55:16,501 --> 00:55:19,004
Don't keep it all bottled up inside!

736
00:55:21,548 --> 00:55:22,758
[sighs]

737
00:55:22,841 --> 00:55:24,092
Seyun.

738
00:55:26,386 --> 00:55:28,513
They were never after you.

739
00:55:29,890 --> 00:55:31,475
What are you talking about?

740
00:55:32,434 --> 00:55:33,935
They were after me.

741
00:55:35,687 --> 00:55:37,230
I'm the one they wanted to kill.
STYLE
::cue()

742
00:55:59,252 --> 00:56:01,171
[phone buzzing]

743
00:56:07,678 --> 00:56:08,679
Yeah.

744
00:56:08,762 --> 00:56:10,222
[♪ tense music playing]

745
00:57:45,358 --> 00:57:48,653
[grunts, choking]

746
00:57:49,905 --> 00:57:51,948
Who are you? [panting]

747
00:57:52,032 --> 00:57:54,117
[straining] Wait, who the hell are you?

748
00:57:54,201 --> 00:57:55,410
[straining]

749
00:57:55,494 --> 00:57:56,536
Hold on.

750
00:57:57,496 --> 00:58:00,916
You had me do all your dirty work,
and now you feign ignorance?

751
00:58:02,167 --> 00:58:03,794
What the hell are you talking about?

752
00:58:04,920 --> 00:58:06,338
I heard about it all.

753
00:58:07,172 --> 00:58:10,175
You tried to kill my wife, didn't you?

754
00:58:11,927 --> 00:58:13,178
[choking]

755
00:58:14,596 --> 00:58:16,014
So what now?

756
00:58:17,891 --> 00:58:20,060
Who will save your wife if I die?

757
00:58:24,606 --> 00:58:27,442
Who else do you think
will save your wife? [grunts]

758
00:58:29,861 --> 00:58:31,905
[straining continues]

759
00:58:42,791 --> 00:58:47,629
THE HUSBAND

760
00:58:47,712 --> 00:58:51,633
[♪ closing theme song playing]

761
00:59:27,752 --> 00:59:31,590
[Taeju] They offered to operate on her
if you killed me.

762
00:59:31,673 --> 00:59:34,259
I'll operate on her.
But I have one condition.

763
00:59:34,342 --> 00:59:36,970
Could Myeonghui really pull this off
all on her own?

764
00:59:37,554 --> 00:59:41,182
What I'll say then is up to you, isn't it?

765
00:59:41,808 --> 00:59:44,686
[Dr. Choi] Kang Taeju.
You've been the problem all along.

766
00:59:44,769 --> 00:59:47,814
There are too many things
that can't be undone.

767
00:59:47,898 --> 00:59:50,442
But we have to make right what we can.

768
00:59:51,109 --> 00:59:53,361
[Manhui] Where's my wife?
I know you took her.

769
00:59:53,445 --> 00:59:56,823
My husband will not let you
get away with this.

770
00:59:56,907 --> 00:59:57,949
[Manhui] Keep your word.

771
00:59:58,033 --> 00:59:59,492
I'll do as you say.

772
01:00:00,076 --> 01:00:02,078
Translated by Hyun Sik Yoon

